  "title": "Ernest Rutherford",
  "summary": "Born in New Zealand in 1871, Rutherford won the 1908 Nobel Prize in Chemistry. At the University of Manchester he held the Langworthy chair from 1907 to 1919; the 1909 Geiger-Marsden experiment there led to his 1911 model of the atom with a central nucleus. He became Cavendish Professor at Cambridge in 1919 and died there in 1937.",
